<SCENARIO VER="105">
{PLAYSND "システム音\The_Lampe.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{MESON "500"}
<TXSPN>Thank you for all your hard work, <VAR NAME="プレイヤー名" unk3="50">-sama. You have reached the ending of the True Meicho Arc.<PG>
............<PG>
I do not know how <VAR NAME="プレイヤー名" unk3="50">-sama felt upon seeing the scenario just now, and the world of Shiyo 900.<PG>
{CHANGECG "立木三日" "グラフィック\イラスト\立木\春花用立ち絵\立木三日目閉じ.gal" "REPEAT" "1" "100" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
However, for my part, I have not the slightest idea what is going on.<PG>
Judging only from the story just now―<PG>
In Shiyo 815, a disaster called the Great Sawa Earthquake occurred.<PG>
From that time on, Motoki-cho was swallowed by giant cherries, its residents perished from deadly gas, and it became a ghost town.<PG>
After that it became a no-entry zone, and even in Shiyo 900, the mystery has not been solved.<PG>
{CHANGECG "立木三日" "グラフィック\イラスト\立木\春花用立ち絵\春花通常.lcm" "REPEAT" "1" "100" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
No... at the very end, we heard someone's voice, did we not?<PG>
It was as though that person had wished for exactly such a disaster.<PG>
It seems that someone with an abominable will exists somewhere in this world.<PG>
If this world showed us that scenario at this moment, perhaps there is a scenario connected to the Great Sawa Earthquake.<PG>
The Great Sawa Earthquake, which occurred in Shiyo 815.<PG>
Shiyo 815 appears to be a major turning point, so let us keep it firmly in mind.<PG>
Now, it seems the next path is opening.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "立木三日" "グラフィック\イラスト\立木\春花用立ち絵\立木三日お辞儀.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "500" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{DELETECG "立木三日,立木ボード,プレート" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{STOPSND "BGM" "3000" "PASS"}
{}
<EVENT VALUE="NOREPAGE">
<EVENT VALUE="MESEND">
